---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Roy Li | Entrepreneur and Public Voice">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Entrepreneur · Community voice · Vancouver-Langara</div>
          <h1>Practical leadership for a province that needs results.</h1>
          <p class="lead">Roy Li is a long-term entrepreneur and public voice focused on responsible government, balanced budgets, public safety, and a stronger environment for business and working families.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/about/">Read Roy’s profile</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="/ideas/">Explore his ideas</a>
          </div>
          <p class="lang-note">This is Roy’s personal website. It is not an official campaign site. 中文信息请见 <a href="/zh/">中文版页面</a>。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-card">
          <div class="portrait-placeholder"></div>
          <h2>Government should be serious, responsible, and grounded in real life.</h2>
          <p>For Roy, politics is not about labels first. It is about whether families feel safe, whether businesses can grow, whether government can pay its bills, and whether citizens can trust public decisions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What Roy is focused on</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Roy is currently sharing his personal background and public-policy views while considering service in Vancouver-Langara. His focus is practical: restore discipline, safety, growth, and trust.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Responsible government</h3><p>British Columbia needs a more conservative approach to government: prudent, restrained, accountable, and focused on results instead of slogans.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Balanced budgets</h3><p>Public money is not abstract. Deficits today become taxes, inflation, or reduced choices tomorrow. A serious government must live within reality.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Public safety</h3><p>Safe streets, safe transit, safe schools, and safe neighbourhoods are the foundation of a functioning society.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
      <div class="quote">“A province cannot build confidence if families feel unsafe, businesses feel punished, and government spends as if consequences do not exist.”</div>
      <div class="list">
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Business and entrepreneurship</strong> Roy understands business from the inside. A healthy province needs entrepreneurs, investment, jobs, and long-term confidence.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Vancouver-Langara</strong> A community of families, professionals, seniors, students, homeowners, renters, and entrepreneurs deserves a serious voice.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Public trust</strong> Government must be able to explain what it is doing, what it costs, and why it works.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta">
        <div>
          <h2>Connect with Roy.</h2>
          <p>For community conversations, media inquiries, or to share issues facing Vancouver-Langara and British Columbia.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
